prompt:
Scenarios: {{inputs.mlx_power_plan}}
Gate results (the sample size check's items named sizes#<scenario id> hold each scenario's sizes as code computed
them): {{gate_results}}

Copy each scenario's sizes into one table the person reads before they confirm the scenarios. You compute nothing:
every cell is copied from the scenario or its sizes item, and code checks each cell against what it computes.
1. title: a plain title with no figures, such as "Sample sizes by scenario".
2. columns, in this order, each with this key and label: scenario "Scenario", power "Power", completers_per_arm
   "Completers per arm", completers_total "Completers in total", recruit_per_arm "To recruit per arm",
   recruit_total "To recruit in total", dropout "Dropout", and sd_used "SD used" when any sizes item gives sd_used.
   No other column, and no figure in the title or a label.
3. rows: one a scenario, in the plan's order, ref its scenario_id, cells in the columns' order:
   - scenario: its label, copied exactly;
   - power and dropout: as percentages (0.8 is 80%, 0.125 is 12.5%, 0 is 0%);
   - completers_per_arm: "<n1> and <n2>", or "one group" when the item gives only a total; completers_total: total;
   - recruit_per_arm: "<recruit1> and <recruit2>", or "one group"; recruit_total: recruit_total;
   - sd_used: the item's sd_used as written (two decimal places), or "not used" when the item gives none;
   - a scenario with no sizes item: "not computed in this run" in each completers and recruit cell.

Previous pass (a repair pass only; null on a first pass):
Table: {{inputs.mlx_sizes_table}}
The person's direction with the failed checks: {{inputs.person_direction}}

On a repair pass, correct each cell the failed checks name to what they say code computed, and change nothing else.
Never cite a check's item names or evidence refs in your text (such as sizes#d30_p80, [sizes_d30_p80] or a finding's id): give the figures and facts plainly, in words a reader understands.
